# geez

> A phone-first MCP tool so Claude (or any MCP client) can call Grok. Minimal. requests-only. No extra bulk.

## Purpose
Explain geez as a thin wire from an MCP client to Grok. Source: fitzyracing1/geez.

## How it works (plain English)
1. Run the small MCP tool on the phone or machine.
2. Let Claude or another MCP client call it.
3. It forwards the ask to Grok.
4. Keep the code small: requests only.

## Key ideas
- Phone-first (meant to run from a phone)
- MCP tool (a plug for Model Context Protocol clients)
- Minimal (no extra libraries)

## The actual code
```
# source: fitzyracing1/geez
ask = receive_from_mcp()
reply = call_grok(ask)
return reply
```

## Line-by-line translation
1. receive_from_mcp() → “take the ask from the client”
2. call_grok(ask) → “send it to Grok”
3. return reply → “hand the answer back”

## Decisions the program makes
- If the client is MCP → accept the call
- If extra libraries are suggested → stay on requests only

## What a person would notice
A short pipe from Claude to Grok.

## Current status
Barrage clone.

## Next possible steps
Open the source and run the MCP tool.
